# Generated by the justfile in the yocto repository, not by hand.
#
#   just image-links      writes recipes-image/
#   just cross-sysroot    writes recipes-sysroot/
#   just cross-arch <cpu> writes conf/current-arch
#
# pool-tumbleweed/ and recipes-microos/ are generated too, by
# `just cross-pool <cpu>`, but they are committed: they are what the image is
# actually built from, and keeping them in the tree is what makes a clone of
# this fork build without a slow regeneration first.
# pool-tumbleweed-riscv64/ is left out on purpose: 205 MB and 50000 files for an
# architecture no image has been built for yet. `just cross-pool riscv64`
# regenerates it. Delete the line below to start tracking it.
pool-tumbleweed-riscv64/

recipes-image/
recipes-sysroot/
conf/current-arch
__pycache__/
